(7036240, 1068214, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m guessing this to be a <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=54446" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Hahn23</a> entry. Right subject, with minimal processing. A bit of tonemapping (just a bit) would probably crank this scene up to DPC mass appeal levels, but I applaud your resistance to what you no doubt feel are gimmicks (gimmicks I use quite routinely, because I like them). I like the scene you managed to capture. I''m sure this was not a quick and casual shot to get. There''s an awful lot in common between photography and hunting, isn''t there?</td>', 'I''m guessing this to be a  Hahn23 entry. Right subject, with minimal processing. A bit of tonemapping (just a bit) would probably crank this scene up to DPC mass appeal levels, but I applaud your resistance to what you no doubt feel are gimmicks (gimmicks I use quite routinely, because I like them). I like the scene you managed to capture. I''m sure this was not a quick and casual shot to get. There''s an awful lot in common between photography and hunting, isn''t there?', '2013-05-12 22:41:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(7036241, 1067734, 83313, '<td valign="top">Just on the chance that nobody else has left this feedback, I''ll drop a critique on this for you and hope it''s appreciated. The reflection looks great, but the top is all grayish in the highlight areas. I suspect the upper area was slightly overexposed and you tried to pull the detail back in with some highlight recovery. Unfortunately, some areas were blown and it just made some unflattering grayish areas. What I don''t know is if you were shooting in JPG or RAW. If RAW, you may have been able to recover the highlight areas with some appropriate techniques. Hope this helped.</td>', 'Just on the chance that nobody else has left this feedback, I''ll drop a critique on this for you and hope it''s appreciated. The reflection looks great, but the top is all grayish in the highlight areas. I suspect the upper area was slightly overexposed and you tried to pull the detail back in with some highlight recovery. Unfortunately, some areas were blown and it just made some unflattering grayish areas. What I don''t know is if you were shooting in JPG or RAW. If RAW, you may have been able to recover the highlight areas with some appropriate techniques. Hope this helped.', '2013-05-12 22:47:33.000000', NULL, 1),
